maybe there would be a hurricane the next period or something damaged to the airline fleet or whatever it was. And that led me to investigate the same kind of prediction error in the context of consumers. And so what I've found in my research is that people are very bad at predicting the idea that something unusual will happen when they don't know what that's going to be. And so maybe like I'm spending extra money this quarter because it's Halloween and I have Halloween decorations. and candy and whatever else. And then suddenly it's like, you know, now it's the next month and it's Thanksgiving, but Thanksgiving doesn't happen again in December. In December, it's Christmas. And then in January, it's New Year's and in February it's, it's Valentine's Day. And so each one of these times,

13
