it's like, well, no, Valentine's Day is not happening again in March, right? So, and each time you're right that that particular expense is not going to recur. And so I think that there's something, thing around the psychology of it's it's very easy to think about what is the baseline set of expenses that we have. So am I going to predict my grocery bills? Yes. Like that's going to be sort of easy to predict my, you know, the cost of my mortgage or my rent. Like, yes, I'm going to do that. And the cost of like, you know, usually I go out to dinner, you know, three times a month and I'm going to plan for that too. So that stuff is sort of stable and it factors very much into our predictions. but what doesn't factor into these predictions are these outlier expenses.

