your credit card bill this month, you could continue to borrow on credit the next month, for example. And I think there's also a question with co-holding of sort of how much money do you have in cash and how much money should you have in cash from a comfort or savings perspective. So I think that there's definitely complexity there, but I think that a lot of what happens with co-holding, and there have been many different explanations proposed largely within the economics literature, I think that there's also something psychological going on where we feel responsible for having money and savings, and we're able to, because of mental accounting, we mentally segregate savings in debt. So we don't think of it as having one pool of money, and that money is basically

