right. Our savings minus our debt. Instead, we think of it as two distinct pools. And so our savings is on the right. Our debt is on the left. And to the extent that you think about these two things as distinct pools, well, what do people who are financially secure have? They have money and savings. And so if I want to feel responsible, I'm going to have money and savings too. And so this is something that I've worked on with work O'Brien looking at what happens. when the amount of the money that you have in savings is designated for different purposes. So if you think about this money that I've set aside in savings for something really responsible, so for my kids' education, for example, I'm not going to touch that.

